Priority: 2
Area: UX
Status: done
Depends on: split-main-into-shell-and-modes

Goal:
Move the shared backend-status readout out of the shell header and anchor it as a workspace overlay in the bottom-right corner.

Context:
The user wants the backend status to behave more like an in-canvas status badge, similar to how the canvas toolbar sits in a workspace corner, instead of occupying header space.

Expected changes:

- move the `#backend-status` element out of the header action flow
- place it inside `#workspace-root`
- style it as a bottom-right overlay with the same non-interactive status-badge behavior across modes
- preserve narrow-screen readability

Acceptance criteria:

- The backend status appears in the bottom-right of the workspace instead of inside the header.
- It does not interfere with pointer interaction in Canvas or PDF mode.
- Responsive CSS still keeps the status readable on smaller windows.
- `npm run build` and `cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` pass.

Notes:

- Keep this slice to layout and placement only.
- Do not widen it into backend-status behavior or copy changes.
